# SQLite feature catalog for the acceptance report.
# area | feature | evidence
# evidence = comma-separated test names (all must pass), or
#            GAP: <why>  (not implemented — counted against completeness)
#            N/A: <why> (the database has no such feature)
#
# SQLite is embedded: the engine is compiled into the driver and every test
# opens real database files (or SQLite's own in-memory databases). There is no
# server to fake, so nothing is mocked.

Opening & configuration | Database file, created on first open; data survives a restart | a_file_database_persists_uses_wal_and_enforces_foreign_keys
Opening & configuration | In-memory database shared by every pooled connection, private to its driver | an_in_memory_database_is_shared_by_the_pool_and_private_to_its_driver, config::tests::two_memory_databases_are_distinct
Opening & configuration | Read-only mode: reads and transactions work, writes refused, no file created; rw mode never creates | read_only_mode_reads_and_refuses_writes, config::tests::setup_skips_writes_when_read_only
Opening & configuration | WAL journal by default (readers never wait for the writer); other journal modes, extra PRAGMAs on every connection | a_file_database_persists_uses_wal_and_enforces_foreign_keys, journal_mode_and_pragmas_are_applied_to_every_connection
Opening & configuration | Foreign keys enforced by default, can be turned off | a_file_database_persists_uses_wal_and_enforces_foreign_keys
Opening & configuration | URL forms (sqlite::memory:, relative, absolute, Windows drive paths) and options (mode, journal_mode, busy_timeout, foreign_keys, synchronous, pool) | config::tests::urls
Opening & configuration | Same engine on every OS (bundled SQLite ≥ 3.38, FTS5 compiled in) | the_bundled_engine_is_the_same_everywhere
Opening & configuration | Network, authentication, TLS | N/A: SQLite is an embedded library reading a local file — no server, no login, nothing on the wire

Concurrency & async | Fully async: every SQLite call on the connection's own thread; a long query leaves the reactor running (proved by a timer ticking during it) | a_long_query_does_not_stall_the_reactor
Concurrency & async | Waiting for another connection's lock (busy timeout) queues without stalling the reactor; a short timeout fails with "database is locked"; WAL readers unaffected | waiting_for_a_lock_queues_without_stalling_and_times_out_cleanly
Concurrency & async | A cancelled / timed-out query is interrupted at once (sqlite3_interrupt) and the connection is free immediately | a_cancelled_query_is_interrupted_and_the_connection_is_free_at_once
Concurrency & async | Writers serialised (BEGIN IMMEDIATE): concurrent read-modify-write transactions lose no update | sqlite_conforms
Concurrency & async | Dropping the driver closes every connection and its file (the file can be deleted — strict on Windows) | dropping_the_driver_closes_its_files

Types | Values typed by declared column type: BOOLEAN, DATE, DATETIME/TIMESTAMP, TIME, JSON, DECIMAL/NUMERIC, INTEGER (i64 min/max), REAL, TEXT (UTF-8, emoji), BLOB, NULL; expressions by stored type; invalid UTF-8 text returned as bytes | values_are_typed_by_the_declared_column_type
Types | Parameters: count checked, u64 beyond i64 refused (no silent rounding), arrays / objects bound as JSON text | parameters_are_checked, values_are_typed_by_the_declared_column_type
Types | Errors: UNIQUE / PRIMARY KEY violations name the column (incl. multi-column keys); foreign key violations; NOT NULL / CHECK as query errors | unique_violations_name_the_column, a_file_database_persists_uses_wal_and_enforces_foreign_keys

ORM (shared layer) | Shared conformance suite (CRUD, values, batch, query builder, binary and long text, unique violation, transactions, row locks, raw SQL, joins/aggregates, execute_many failure semantics, cursors, cancelled transactions) | sqlite_conforms
ORM (shared layer) | A transaction abandoned half-way (timeout) commits nothing and never hands an open transaction to the next caller | sqlite_conforms
ORM (shared layer) | Batch insert with generated keys (one multi-row INSERT) | sqlite_conforms
ORM (shared layer) | Select builder: INNER / LEFT JOIN, GROUP BY, aggregates, HAVING, ORDER BY, LIMIT / OFFSET (incl. OFFSET without LIMIT) | sqlite_conforms
ORM (shared layer) | Transactions: commit, rollback on error, hand-written SQL inside them | sqlite_conforms
ORM (shared layer) | Row-level locks (SELECT … FOR UPDATE) | N/A: SQLite locks the whole database; IMMEDIATE transactions give the same no-lost-update guarantee (sqlite_conforms)

Hand-written SQL | Any query with bound parameters, results typed by column, mapped onto entities by name | sqlite_conforms
Hand-written SQL | UPSERT (ON CONFLICT … DO UPDATE), RETURNING, window functions | hand_written_sql_has_upsert_returning_and_window_functions
Hand-written SQL | Cursors: batches on demand, two open at once in one transaction, other statements in between, released with the transaction | cursors_and_streams_never_hold_the_whole_result, sqlite_conforms
Hand-written SQL | Streaming 200k rows without collecting; a callback error stops cleanly and the connection works on | cursors_and_streams_never_hold_the_whole_result
Hand-written SQL | execute_many under one savepoint: same outcome as row by row on a failure part-way, one commit for the batch | sqlite_conforms, online_backup_copies_a_consistent_database
Hand-written SQL | Scripts (several statements, triggers with BEGIN … END); an error stops the script | execute_script_runs_triggers_and_multi_statement_scripts

SQLite features | Full-text search (FTS5, Unicode tokenizer with diacritics folded, ranking, highlight) | full_text_search_and_json_functions_are_built_in
SQLite features | JSON functions (json_extract, json_each) over bound JSON parameters | full_text_search_and_json_functions_are_built_in
SQLite features | Rust functions callable from SQL (fixed and variadic arguments, deterministic — usable in an index; errors reach the caller); call_function | rust_functions_are_callable_from_sql
SQLite features | Online backup of a live database (file or in-memory) to a file | online_backup_copies_a_consistent_database
SQLite features | Stored procedures | N/A: SQLite has no procedural language — Rust functions take their place (call() answers Unsupported: rust_functions_are_callable_from_sql)
SQLite features | Incremental BLOB I/O: a 5 MiB BLOB filled 64 KiB at a time in place, a piece read across chunks; never grows; names are not SQL | incremental_blob_io_reads_and_writes_pieces_in_place
SQLite features | Change hooks: every inserted / updated / deleted row through any pooled connection, commits and rollbacks | change_hooks_report_every_row_and_transaction_end
SQLite features | Serialize a whole database to bytes (a valid database file) and open an in-memory copy from bytes (WAL images included) | a_database_serializes_to_bytes_and_opens_from_them
SQLite features | Native extensions loaded into every connection (a real extension built by the test: .so / .dylib / .dll), named entry points, load failures fail the open; SQL's own load_extension() stays refused | a_native_extension_is_loaded_into_every_connection, a_named_entry_point_and_load_failures
SQLite features | Change capture (session extension): a transaction's changes as a changeset, replayed on another database, only tracked tables, nothing from before / after | a_transaction_recorded_on_one_database_replays_on_another
SQLite features | Changesets inverted to undo; patchsets (smaller, not invertible); concatenated into their net effect | the_inverse_undoes_the_transaction, patchsets_are_smaller_and_changesets_concatenate
SQLite features | Applying with conflicts: abort (nothing applied), skip, replace — conflicts counted | conflicts_abort_skip_or_replace
SQLite features | A failed or abandoned (timed-out) capture never leaks into a later one | a_failed_or_abandoned_transaction_records_nothing_later
SQLite features | Encryption at rest | N/A: not part of SQLite (SQLCipher / SEE are separate products)

Platform & runtime | Runs on Linux: whole driver suite (CI) | ci::test_ubuntu_latest
Platform & runtime | Runs on macOS: whole driver suite (CI) | ci::test_macos_latest
Platform & runtime | Runs on Windows: whole driver suite, incl. file release on drop (CI) | ci::test_windows_latest
